From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 17:38:46 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 84/84] runner: the reply's receipt lists the digit stops that
 fired, so a reply the runner cut says so

A digit stop replaces a drawn reasoning token with a newline: after an owned value, after the inline mark, or past
TF_RUNNER_DIGIT_RUN_MAX (1024 digits). Only the serving log recorded it. The reply's runner receipt (the response's
tensorfold.runner) counted cells alone, so a reply whose only runner action was a stop read as "runner idle": all
cell counts 0, cells []. In the 11-14 opencode A/B on Qwen3.8-Flash-Next TP1 one lanes-on reply (fib(250) by hand)
had its model-written 1,024-digit reasoning run cut by the run cap, then closed its reasoning there and answered
without a tool call; its receipt said nothing, and the A/B report concluded the lanes were not involved.

The stop state counts each fired stop by its reason (the same events as the serving log's "digit stop" lines) and the
receipt adds "stops":{"after_value":N,"after_mark":N,"run_cap":N} after resume_ms when any fired. A reply with no
stop keeps its receipt byte for byte, so the existing receipt fixtures are unchanged.

Tests: a session whose reasoning run reaches a cap of 8 lists run_cap 1 with every cell count 0; one digit short
(negative control) no stop fires and the receipt ends as before.
